# .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Who must approve a pull request that changes a path, when the `Main` ruleset has
# "Require review from Code Owners" on. Until that setting is on, this file only
# makes GitHub request a review; it blocks nothing. Read docs/setup/repository-settings.md
# before you turn the setting on: with one owner who also opens the pull requests,
# it blocks every pull request that touches an owned path.
#
# Rules of this file format: the LAST matching line wins. A line with a pattern
# and no owner removes the owner. Paths are case sensitive. `!` and `[ ]` do not
# work. A wrong or unknown owner name gives NO owner (it fails open), so check the
# file after each edit:
#   gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/codeowners/errors
#
# This file follows rail 8 of .github/workflows/automerge.yml (CONTENT / NOT_CONTENT).
# Change the two together. They differ in two ways:
#   - Stricter here: /docs/setup/ (commands that the owner runs as administrator)
#     and /detections/sigma/LICENSE.md have an owner. Rail 8 treats them as content.
#   - Weaker here: rail 8 matches its exclusions (Python files, research/tools/,
#     .github/, a `.claude` entry, the agent-instruction files, docs/CODEOWNERS) in
#     any letter case, and a technique directory as `T` and digits. This file can
#     name exact spellings only. Block 4 names the usual ones. A different
#     spelling (aGENTS.md) has NO owner here: only rail 8 holds it, and rail 8
#     binds only the automerge workflow.
#
# In a fork: replace every @vasquja with your own login. The upstream owner has no
# write access to your fork, so the upstream name protects nothing there.

# 1. Default: every path has an owner. A new path that no later line names needs
#    the owner's approval (fail closed).
*                                    @vasquja

# 2. Content: rules, cases, fixtures, TRRs and docs. No owner, so no review is needed.
#    `T*` is the nearest pattern to a technique ID (T1537, T1552.005): a rule file in
#    a directory that does not start with `T` keeps the owner.
*.md
/detections/sigma/T*/*.yml
/detections/sigma/T*/*.cases.jsonl
/detections/cloud/fixtures/*/*.json
/detections/benign/scores.json
/research/
/docs/
/upstream/

# 3. Checking code, agent policy, setup guides and licence texts inside the content
#    paths. These lines must stay below block 2.
*.py                                 @vasquja
/research/tools/                     @vasquja
/.github/                            @vasquja
.claude/                             @vasquja
**/.claude                           @vasquja
AGENTS.md                            @vasquja
CLAUDE.md                            @vasquja
CLAUDE.local.md                      @vasquja
/docs/CODEOWNERS                     @vasquja
/docs/setup/                         @vasquja
/detections/sigma/LICENSE.md         @vasquja

# 4. Usual other spellings of the agent policy names. On a file system that is not
#    case sensitive (macOS, Windows) an agent reads them as the names in block 3.
#    This list cannot be complete. These lines must stay below block 2.
agents.md                            @vasquja
Agents.md                            @vasquja
claude.md                            @vasquja
Claude.md                            @vasquja
claude.local.md                      @vasquja
Claude.local.md                      @vasquja
.Claude/                             @vasquja
**/.Claude                           @vasquja
